[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951745746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121285#issuecomment-4951745746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121285","id":4951745746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJyWk0g","user":{"login":"TrueJole","id":121569485,"node_id":"U_kgDOBz8AzQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121569485?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueJole","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T15:35:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T15:36:19Z","body":"I don't know enough to know the expected behaviour, but this is what I get on master:\n\n<img width=\"1196\" height=\"690\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87cb4e8a-124c-4a93-8299-8f41100e8653\" />\n\n```sh\nOpTypeAccelerationStructureKHR is not supported yet.\ntriangle pixel (push constant): 0.00 1.00 0.00\nbackground pixel (push constant): 1.00 0.00 0.00\n```\n\n```\nGodot v4.8.dev (2c089e9bf) - Fedora Linux 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 5 9600X 6-Core Processor (6 threads) - 30.45 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n```\n\nSame if I flip USB_UB0 to `true`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951745746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951801341","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121285#issuecomment-4951801341","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121285","id":4951801341,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJyZ9_Q","user":{"login":"pockerhead","id":28385842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mzg1ODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28385842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead","html_url":"https://github.com/pockerhead","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T15:50:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T15:50:58Z","body":"Thanks for testing! Very useful data point. I just ran the **exact same commit** (2c089e9bf, CI artifact) on my machine — push constants still read zeros here, so it's vendor-dependent rather than fixed on master:\n\n| Engine | GPU / driver | push constant | UBO control |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| v4.7.stable | RTX 4070 Ti, NVIDIA 32.0.15.9621, Windows 11 | zeros | works |\n| master 2c089e9bf | RTX 4070 Ti (same machine) | zeros | works |\n| master 2c089e9bf | RX 9070 XT, RADV, Fedora | works | works |\n\nI believe I found the root cause. In `servers/rendering/rendering_shader_container.cpp` (~L310), the `PIPELINE_TYPE_RAYTRACING` branch ORs the shader stage enum **ordinals** instead of the `_BIT` flags:\n\n```cpp\nuniform_stage_flags = RDC::SHADER_STAGE_RAYGEN |   // = 5, not (1 << 5)\n        RDC::SHADER_STAGE_ANY_HIT |                // = 6\n        RDC::SHADER_STAGE_CLOSEST_HIT |            // = 7\n        RDC::SHADER_STAGE_MISS |                   // = 8\n        RDC::SHADER_STAGE_INTERSECTION;            // = 9\n// 5|6|7|8|9 == 15 == VERTEX_BIT | FRAGMENT_BIT | TESSELATION_CONTROL_BIT | TESSELATION_EVALUATION_BIT\n```\n\nSo for raytracing pipelines `push_constant_stages` ends up with VERTEX/FRAGMENT/TESSELLATION bits, and the Vulkan driver builds `VkPushConstantRange.stageFlags` / calls `vkCmdPushConstants` with **no RT stage bits at all** (the `RD_STAGE_TO_VK_SHADER_STAGE_BITS` table in `rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp` is correct — it just receives the wrong mask). Reading push constants from a stage not covered by any range is undefined behavior per the Vulkan spec — NVIDIA reads zeros, RADV happens to deliver the data, which matches the table above. The same wrong mask also feeds descriptor `stageFlags`, which drivers tolerate in practice — that would explain why the UBO path works everywhere.\n\nThe fix looks like a one-liner: use the `SHADER_STAGE_*_BIT` constants in that branch.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951801341/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956473417","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121285#issuecomment-4956473417","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121285","id":4956473417,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ23ISQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T09:29:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T09:29:15Z","body":"Are you using AI to write your issue reports and comments?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956473417/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956685871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121285#issuecomment-4956685871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121285","id":4956685871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ3EGLw","user":{"login":"pockerhead","id":28385842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mzg1ODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28385842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead","html_url":"https://github.com/pockerhead","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pockerhead/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T09:53:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T09:53:36Z","body":"Hi! Yes — I use AI-assisted development; in this case AI was used for the RT experiment itself and for testing hypotheses about these bugs.\n\nSorry, I missed the recent AI policy update. To be clear about the split: both bugs were caught by me on my own hardware during my RT work, and I ran the MRPs myself before filing — every number in the tables is an actual readback from my machine (including the master CI-artifact run). The root-cause analysis was AI-assisted (navigating the engine source), and I verified it against the actual code and behavior. AI was also used to prepare the English texts, since I'm not a native speaker — this reply too is my own words, written in Russian and translated.\n\nEvery claim was re-checked against primary sources (engine source, Vulkan spec, real runs) before filing. I'm happy to rewrite the reports in my own words or in whatever format the policy requires — just tell me what's preferred.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{